  "name": "Question 14",
  "problem": "Find $\\,|\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & x & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 5 & y & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}|$ given that $\\,|\\begin{aligned}x & -1 \\\\ 5 & y\\end{aligned}|=-3.$",
  "worked_solution": "Notice that we have a block upper triangular matrix. Therefore, its determinant is equal to the product of the diagonal blocks' determinants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & x & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 5 & y & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}| & =|\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & x & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 5 & y & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =6\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}x & -1 \\\\ 5 & y\\end{aligned}|\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =6\\cdot (-3)\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =-90.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
